{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Orxta","id":"343605682580488215","is_bot":0,"username":"robdor."},"author_id":"343605682580488215","channel_id":"748222087226982401","content":"I had a choose-your-own-adventure idea about the weekly themes. Each week the main event would have an obvious fail/succeed condition. This would affect the week directly after. I'm thinking the main faction of each borough will be greatly influenced by the outcome. \nFor example\nWeek 1, all factions are vying for power, and the players will influence which two factions emerge as the economic or political powerhouse. \nWeek 2, the two main factions wage espionage wars with each other, and players influence which emerges victorious.\nWeek 3, one factions is on top, and \"the villain\" is running this faction. At the end of week three, if the villain is defeated, the faction commits to independence. If players fail to defeat the villain, the faction joins the redcoats. \nWeek 4, Players must try to gather more support for the war effort since the revolution is on now. This affects the whether the revolution or redcoats controls Fort Washington.\nWeek 5, no real decisions to make. Ft Washington is saved or not. The rebellion succeeds, or not.\n\nThese decisions should affect every part of the world. Including stock values of various companies, access to certain types of airships, weapons, allies. Players may have to turn against their boroughs. Others may become their local leaders.","created_at":"2020-12-23T16:01:21.475000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"791334644247035934","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
